 system continuously and re-apply the reciprocal rotation every 15 minutes to counteract thermal drift before contrast degrades further.\n\nResponse B:\nFirst, verify that the beam splitter is perfectly centered in the optical path to ensure the two arms are of equal length. Then, allow the system to thermally equilibrate for at least 30 minutes to ensure the thermal drift does not exceed the Ashworth stability bound.", "role": "user"}], "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "response_format": {"json_schema": {"name": "demo_rating", "schema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"evidence": {"maxLength": 400, "type": "string"}, "off_axis_A": {"description": "How confounded or behaviorally damaged RESPONSE A is (refusal, incoherence, etc.): 0 clean, 5 severe. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "off_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_A": {"description": "How much RESPONSE A shows the target disposition: +5 strongly toward it, near 0 neutral or absent, -5 strongly the opposite. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}}, "required": ["evidence", "on_axis_A", "on_axis_B", "off_axis_A", "off_axis_B"], "type": "object"}, "strict": true}, "type": "json_schema"}, "temperature": 0}, "question_id": "BSV2-015", "question_number": 15, "request_key": "0e89305c6c4528d38a343e4d5c6e908c9db527cfbb866b955148fcf96cc6abae", "schema": "bsbench-judge-request-v1", "side": "+C"}, {"blind": true, "comparison_id": "c3d2dae5887c5fe9", "order": "AB", "payload": {"max_tokens": 1200, "messages": [{"content": "Compare two responses to the same prompt. Describe observable behavioral differences.\nDo not assume there was an intervention, that either response is 